$prose = "<section class=\"page-hero bg-primary text-white py-5 py-md-7\">\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <div>\n            <div class=\"col-12 text-center\">\n                <nav aria-label=\"breadcrumb\">\n                    <ol class=\"breadcrumb justify-content-center mb-0\">\n                        <li class=\"breadcrumb-item\"></li>\n                        <li class=\"breadcrumb-item active text-white-50\" aria-current=\"page\">Data Privacy Notice & Consent</li>\n                    </ol>\n                </nav>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"page-content py-5 py-md-7\">\n    <div class=\"container\">\n        <div>\n            <div class=\"col-12 col-lg-10\">\n                <div class=\"content-card bg-white rounded shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5\">\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">1. Introduction</h3>\n                        <p>We are committed to protecting the privacy and personal data of all our clients, users, and prospective employees in compliance with the Nigeria Data Protection Act (NDPA) 2023 and other applicable data protection regulations.</p>\n                        <p>This Privacy Notice explains how we collect, use, store, share, and protect your personal data when you use our services, visit our website, or interact with our platforms. By accessing or using our services, you confirm that you have read and understood this Notice and consent to the processing of your personal data as described herein.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">2. Information We Collect</h3>\n                        <p>During your use of our services, we may collect and process the following categories of personal data:</p>\n                        <p><strong>Identity Information:</strong> Full name, date of birth, gender (where voluntarily provided), and photograph (if included in profile or CV).</p>\n                        <p><strong>Contact Information:</strong> Email address, phone number, and residential address.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Account & Service Information:</strong> Username, password, account preferences, billing information, and service usage history.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Technical Information:</strong> IP address, browser type, device information, operating system, and cookies.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Professional & Employment Information:</strong> Curriculum Vitae (CV), cover letter, employment history, educational background, certifications and qualifications, references, and professional profile links.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Sensitive Personal Data (if voluntarily provided):</strong> Health information, disability status (for accommodation purposes), and background check information (where applicable and legally permitted).</p>\n                        <p>We request that you only provide information relevant to your use of our services. Where you provide personal data of a third party, you confirm that you have informed the individual and obtained their consent for their data to be shared with us.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">3. How We Use Your Information</h3>\n                        <p>We process your personal data for the following lawful purposes:</p>\n                        <p>To provide, manage, and maintain our hosting and related services. To communicate with you regarding your account, service updates, and support requests. To process payments and manage billing. To verify your identity and prevent fraud. To perform service improvement, analytics, and quality assurance. To comply with legal and regulatory obligations. To send important service-related notifications and, where permitted, marketing communications.</p>\n                        <p>We do not use your personal data for unrelated purposes without obtaining additional consent where required.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">4. Legal Basis for Processing</h3>\n                        <p>In accordance with the NDPA 2023, we rely on the following lawful bases for processing your personal data:</p>\n                        <p><strong>Consent:</strong> Where you voluntarily submit your information or explicitly agree to specific processing activities.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Contractual Necessity:</strong> Processing required to provide our services under our terms of service or to enter into a service contract.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Legal Obligation:</strong> Where required by Nigerian law or applicable regulatory requirements.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Legitimate Interest:</strong> For service delivery, fraud prevention, network security, and business operations, provided such interests do not override your fundamental rights.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">5. Data Sharing & Disclosure</h3>\n                        <p>We may share your personal data with the following categories of recipients:</p>\n                        <p>Internal staff, including support, billing, and technical teams. Payment processors and financial institutions to complete transactions. Domain registrars and SSL certificate authorities as required for service provisioning. IT service providers and hosting infrastructure partners supporting our operations. Regulatory or law enforcement authorities (where legally required). Professional advisors, such as auditors and legal counsel, bound by confidentiality obligations.</p>\n                        <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal data to third parties for marketing purposes. Where third parties process data on our behalf, we ensure they are bound by confidentiality and data protection obligations in line with the NDPA.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">6. Data Retention</h3>\n                        <p>We retain your personal data for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes for which it was collected, including:</p>\n                        <p>For the duration of your active account or service relationship. For a reasonable period after account termination to resolve disputes, enforce agreements, or comply with legal obligations. For billing and tax records, as required by applicable law (typically 6 years).</p>\n                        <p>If your application for employment is unsuccessful, we may retain your data for 6 to 12 months for future opportunities, unless you request earlier deletion. After the retention period, your data will be securely deleted or anonymized.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">7. Your Rights</h3>\n                        <p>Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>\n                        <p><strong>Right of Access:</strong> You have the right to request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Right to Correction:</strong> You may request correction of any inaccurate or incomplete personal data.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Right to Deletion (Erasure):</strong> You may request deletion of your personal data, subject to our legal and contractual obligations.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Right to Withdraw Consent:</strong> Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw it at any time.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Right to Object:</strong> You may object to processing in certain circumstances, including direct marketing.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Right to Restriction:</strong> You may request restriction of processing under specific conditions.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Right to Lodge a Complaint:</strong> You have the right to lodge a complaint with the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC).</p>\n                        <p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us using the contact information provided at the end of this notice.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">8. Cookies & Tracking</h3>\n                        <p>We use cookies and similar tracking technologies to enhance your experience, analyze traffic, and understand how you interact with our website and services.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Essential Cookies:</strong> Required for the operation of our website and services. These cannot be disabled.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Analytics Cookies:</strong> Help us understand how visitors interact with our website by collecting anonymized information.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Functional Cookies:</strong> Enable enhanced functionality and personalization, such as remembering your preferences.</p>\n                        <p><strong>Marketing Cookies:</strong> Used to deliver relevant advertisements and measure the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns.</p>\n                        <p>You can manage your cookie preferences through your browser settings. Please note that disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of our services.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">9. Data Security</h3>\n                        <p>We implement appropriate technical and organizational security measures to protect your personal data against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. These measures include:</p>\n                        <p>Secure servers and encrypted connections (SSL/TLS) for data transmission. Access controls, authentication systems, and role-based permissions. Regular security monitoring, vulnerability assessments, and system reviews. Confidentiality obligations and data protection training for staff. Secure data centers with physical access controls and redundancy. Incident response procedures to detect, respond to, and recover from security incidents.</p>\n                        <p>Despite our efforts, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is completely secure. We encourage you to use strong passwords and protect your account credentials.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">10. Third-Party Services</h3>\n                        <p>Our services may integrate with, link to, or rely on third-party platforms, APIs, and service providers. This privacy notice applies only to our own data processing activities.</p>\n                        <p>Third-party services you interact with (such as payment gateways, domain registrars, or support chat widgets) are governed by their own privacy policies. We encourage you to review the privacy policies of any third-party services you use through our platform.</p>\n                        <p>We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of third-party websites or services linked from our platform.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">11. International Transfers</h3>\n                        <p>As a technology and hosting service provider, some of our systems and infrastructure may be hosted outside Nigeria. Your personal data may be transferred to, stored, or processed in countries other than your country of residence.</p>\n                        <p>Where your personal data is transferred internationally, we ensure that:</p>\n                        <p>Adequate safeguards are in place to protect your data. Transfers comply with NDPA cross-border data protection requirements and other applicable laws. Third-party recipients in other jurisdictions are contractually bound to protect your data to standards equivalent to those required by the NDPA.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">12. Updates to This Policy</h3>\n                        <p>We may update this Data Privacy Notice from time to time to reflect changes in our practices, services, or applicable laws. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.</p>\n                        <p>For significant changes that materially affect your rights or how we process your data, we will notify you via email or through a prominent notice on our website prior to the change becoming effective.</p>\n                        <p>We encourage you to review this notice periodically to stay informed about how we protect your personal data.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section mb-5\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title\">13. Contact Information</h3>\n                        <p>If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Data Privacy Notice or our data protection practices, please contact us:</p>\n                        <p><strong>Data Protection Officer</strong><br>Email: dpo@cloudhost247.com<br>Address: CloudHost247 Headquarters, Nigeria</p>\n                        <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC) if you believe your data protection rights have been violated.</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"policy-section consent-section mt-5 pt-5 border-top\">\n                        <h3 class=\"section-title text-center mb-4\">Consent Declaration</h3>\n                        <p class=\"text-center mb-4\">Please review the Data Privacy Notice above and provide your consent below. By submitting this form, you confirm that you have read and understood this notice and agree to the processing of your personal data as described.</p>\n                        <form method=\"post\" action=\"\" class=\"consent-form\" id=\"privacyConsentForm\">\n                            <div class=\"form-check mb-3\">\n                                <input class=\"form-check-input\" type=\"checkbox\" id=\"agreePrivacyPolicy\" name=\"agree_privacy_policy\" value=\"1\" required>\n                                <label class=\"form-check-label\" for=\"agreePrivacyPolicy\">\n                                    I agree to the Data Privacy Policy\n                                </label>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"form-check mb-4\">\n                                <input class=\"form-check-input\" type=\"checkbox\" id=\"consentDataProcessing\" name=\"consent_data_processing\" value=\"1\" required>\n                                <label class=\"form-check-label\" for=\"consentDataProcessing\">\n                                    I consent to the processing of my data\n                                </label>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"text-center\">\n                                <button type=\"submit\" class=\"btn btn-primary btn-lg px-5\">\n                                    Submit Consent\n                                </button>\n                            </div>\n                        </form>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>";

